# Line endings for Go source.
#
# The repository stores LF. With core.autocrlf=true on Windows, git checks Go
# files out as CRLF, and gofmt then reports every one of them as unformatted -
# so `gofmt -l .` passed or failed depending on whether git happened to have
# touched the file recently. Pinning the working tree to LF makes the check
# mean the same thing for everyone.
*.go text eol=lf

# Keep diffs honest for the files where a stray CRLF would matter most.
*.md text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# Generated or binary: never line-ending translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gguf binary
